# Code_Aster Command File - Generated by MecwayAsterBridge
# Template for CALC_MODES: modal analysis (Mecway V30, natural frequencies
# and mode shapes) and linear buckling (Mecway B30, buckling load factors
# and buckling shapes). Filled in via str.format() from bridge_to_aster.py
# (_build_modal).
#
# Placeholders (name between single braces):
#   defigroup_block   -> DEFI_GROUP / CREA_MAILLAGE / MODI_MAILLAGE (as in
#                        MECA_STATIQUE)
#   model_block       -> AFFE_MODELE per elset
#   cara_elem_block   -> AFFE_CARA_ELEM (beams, shells, springs, point masses)
#   materials_block   -> DEFI_MATERIAU per material (with RHO)
#   fieldmat_block    -> AFFE_MATERIAU assignment
#   loads_block       -> AFFE_CHAR_MECA's: modal without prestress only
#                        the supports and couplings; buckling and modal with
#                        prestress also the loads
#   static_block      -> buckling and modal with prestress: MECA_STATIQUE with
#                        all loads and the stress field SIEF_ELGA from it;
#                        modal without prestress: comment
#   assemblage_block  -> ASSEMBLAGE: stiffness (RIGI_MECA) and mass
#                        (MASS_MECA) and/or geometric stiffness
#                        (RIGI_GEOM); with prestress also RIGI_ROTA
#                        (centrifugal) and COMB_MATR_ASSE K + Kg
#   calc_modes_block  -> res = CALC_MODES(...)
#   export_block      -> aster_results_export (Mecway results: one
#                        <mode> per mode shape/buckling shape)
#   impr_resu_block   -> IMPR_RESU MED (only with "med_export")
#
# A brace that is not a placeholder: double it ({ or }).

# Language of the messages of the job scripts (aster_*.py)
